cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Running Cogni-Brain (GLM-5.3-Flash) on NVIDIA DGX Spark with llama.cpp and MTP Speculative Decoding"
message: "If this benchmark harness helps your work, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Rawat"
    given-names: "Rajendra Singh"
    affiliation: "cogni.chat"
repository-code: "https://github.com/airawatraj/dgx-spark-glm53-flash-agent"
abstract: >-
  A production-ready technical benchmarking suite for running unsloth/GLM-5.3-Flash-GGUF
  (320B total params, 18B active MoE) on a single NVIDIA DGX Spark (GB10 Grace-Blackwell,
  128 GB unified memory) served as Cogni-Brain in container spark-brain via llama.cpp
  with native Blackwell sm_121a compilation, MTP speculative decoding, and quantized KV caching.
keywords:
  - "GLM-5.3-Flash"
  - "ox-alpha"
  - "Cogni-Brain"
  - "DGX Spark"
  - "GB10"
  - "Grace Blackwell"
  - "llama.cpp"
  - "GGUF"
  - "MTP"
  - "Speculative Decoding"
  - "AI Agents"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-09"
